, adaptability.\n\nLet's assess each:\n\nA: reliability 100% (strong). Decision quality: can make correct decisions quickly (strong). Crew cooperation: creates positive atmosphere (good). Communication: difficulty communicating ideas (weak). Egocentric (maybe weak for teamwork). Not willing to further education (weak adaptability). Overall strong reliability and decision but weak communication and adaptability.\n\nB: conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence), excellent computer skills (technical). But can be grumpy and uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). So strengths but teamwork concerns.\n\nC: anticipates dangerous situations (stress resilience, decision), sees complex connections (technical), excellent spatial vision (technical), very good leadership (crew cooperation), but not good at taking criticism (adaptability), unorganized (attention). So strong technical and leadership but concerns on adaptability and organization.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress), concentrates well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical/decision), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but arrogant (crew cooperation), weak leadership (crew). So mixed.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? Need balanced across criteria, not overvalue one strength. A has reliability and decision but communication issues. B has reliability, stress, technical but cooperation issues. C has technical and leadership but adaptability and organization issues. D has problem solving and responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nProbably B might be strong overall but cooperation concerns could be serious. A's communication difficulty could be critical for cockpit communication. C's unorganized could affect attention. D's arrogance could affect crew.\n\nMaybe B is best despite uncooperative? But uncooperative is a big issue for crew. A's egocentric also problematic.\n\nC's leadership and anticipation may be valuable for long-distance flights. Unorganized may be mitigated with procedures. Not good at criticism could affect training.\n\nWe need to pick a provisional recommendation. I think Candidate C seems strong on technical, decision, stress, leadership, but concerns on adaptability and organization. Could be addressed. Others have more severe crew cooperation issues (B uncooperative, A communication difficulty, D arrogant). So I will recommend Candidate C.\n\nNow produce public message stating recommendation for Candidate C, referencing discussion (none yet) but we can say \"Considering the need for technical competence and decision-making, I think C stands out\". Provide evidence: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, very good leadership. Also note concerns: not good at criticism, unorganized, but still overall best.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
